course: dictionary
lesson: 3519
title: Faux: fake, not real
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Faux is an adjective that means fake, or made to look like the real thing. You will mostly meet it with materials such as fur, leather or marble. Look at the words around it: «faux fur» and «faux leather» are made without real animals, so faux tells you the thing is a copy.
explain: The word is borrowed from French, where «faux» means «false». Ask yourself: is this the real thing, or a copy that only looks real? If the answer is copy, faux is the word you need.
explain: Be careful with French words that look like English ones. «Faux amis» means false friends: words that look like English words but mean something different. Faux itself is a word that tells you something is not what it seems.
fact: Faux means fake, or made to look like the real thing.
fact: «Faux fur» and «faux leather» are made without real animals.
fact: A «faux finish» makes paint look like wood or stone.
fact: «Faux pas» means an embarrassing mistake in manners, and it comes from French.
fact: Faux is borrowed from French, where «faux» means «false».
exercise: «The coat has a collar of faux fur.» What does faux mean here? | Very soft and warm, from a real animal | *Fake, made to look like real fur | Brand new | Wet and muddy
exercise: «A faux finish makes paint look like wood or stone.» What does a faux finish do? | *Makes paint look like wood or stone | Makes the paint glow | Makes the wood wet | Removes paint from the walls
exercise: Faux comes from French. In French, «faux» means what? | *False | Fur | Soft | Fast
test: «Faux fur» is made without what? | Warmth | *Real animals | Thread | Buttons
test: «Faux pas» means what? | *An embarrassing mistake in manners | A famous painting | A big party | A fast walk
exam: «Faux amis» means what in English? | Best friends | *False friends | New friends | Old friends
